4. Learned advocate for the petitioners submits that the proceedings is found to be beyond purview and scope of section 498(A), 323, 504 and 114 of the IPC and under Section 3 and 4 of the Prohibition of Dowry Act coupled with the fact that the petitioners are not directly or indirectly involved in the alleged offence.
It appears that petitioners are facing charge of Section 498A of IPC.
In this regard, it would be apposite to refer the decisions of the Apex Court in case of Abhishek vs. State of Madhya Pradesh reported in 2023INSC779 / (Criminal Appeal No. 1457 of 2015); Preeti Gupta and another vs. State of Jharkhand and another [(2010) 7 SCC 667];
